<title>UK: JFS sets 450 million mark five-year bond.</title>
<headline>JFS sets 450 million mark five-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Bank of Tokyo Mitsubishi (Deutschland) and Deutsche Morgan Grenfell.</p>
<p> BORROWER   JAPAN FINANCE CORP FOR SMALL BUSINESS (JFS)</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  JAPAN (RATED AAA/AAA)</p>
<p> AMT    450 MLN DEM   COUPON     4.5	 MATURITY    07.AUG.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.685   PAY DATE    07.AUG.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.25	REOFFER    99.685    SPREAD	+20 BP</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  =	   LISTING    FFT	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/JP/DE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  JAPAN     TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.75	LIST FEE    0.25</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND FEB 2002 BOBL</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
